@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Add or update your default shipping address - Lively Help Center";
    ViewData["CategorySlug"] = "Buying";
    ViewData["SubCategorySlug"] = "Getting Started";
    ViewData["HeroTitle"] = "Add or update your default shipping address";
    ViewData["HeroStyle"] = "background-image: linear-gradient(rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.4), rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.4)), url('/img/contact_area/contact_hero_bg.png');";
    ViewData["IsArticle"] = true;
}

<div class="article-detail-page">
    <div class="article-body">
        <p>Your default shipping address is where all your future orders will be sent. You can update your default shipping address anytime before you buy. Make sure it's correct so your order arrives at the right place.</p>

        <p><strong>Change your default shipping address in app:</strong></p>
        <ol>
            <li>Tap Account</li>
            <li>Scroll down and tap Addresses</li>
            <li>Tap the + icon, or choose a saved address to edit or delete</li>
        </ol>

        <p><strong>Change your default shipping address on web:</strong></p>
        <ol>
            <li>From Lively.com, click your account icon in the top right</li>
            <li>Under the Buying tab, select Account Settings</li>
            <li>Click Addresses on the left</li>
            <li>Click Add, or use the ... icon next to an address to edit or delete</li>
        </ol>

        <div class="article-info-box">
            <strong>Tip:</strong> If you're watching a show, tap the Wallet icon > Shipping to make a quick change. Updates from here will apply to future orders too.
        </div>

        <p>Need to fix the address for an existing order? <a href="#">How to change your order's shipping address.</a></p>

        <div class="helpful-widget">
            <p>Was this article helpful?</p>
            <div class="helpful-buttons">
                <button type="button">Yes</button>
                <button type="button">No</button>
            </div>
            <span>80 out of 145 found this helpful</span>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
